SUMMARY:Love\, Simon (2018): Laugh Out Loud Pride Film Screening NEW
DESCRIPTION:This is a free Adult School class. Click below to 
 register.\n\nJoin us for a screening the 2019 GLAAD Media Award Winner\, 
 "Love\, Simon\," to wrap up Pride this year at Montclair Public Library! 
 The screening will be followed by a open panel discussion about the film 
 featuring queer film makers Mac Allen\, Erby Beauvil and FDU Professor 
 Cordelia Siporin.  Free popcorn will be provided by The Claridge. These 
 screenings are proudly co-presented by Pride Center of Montclair. Come join 
 in the fun and bring a friend!\n\n"Seventeen-year-old Simon keeps a huge 
 secret from his family\, his friends and all of his classmates: he's gay. 
 When that secret is threatened by a blackmailer\, Simon must come to terms 
 with his identity." Rated TV-14
LOCATION:Montclair Main - Auditorium\, Montclair Public Library
ORGANIZER;CN="Montclair Adult School":MAILTO:adultschool@montclairlibrary.org
CATEGORIES:Adult School, Books, Film & Theater, Teen Services
