SUMMARY:Unearthing Stories of Female Artists in Exile and Resistance: Persepolis
DESCRIPTION:Session one of a two-part discussion series exploring the 
 graphic memoirs of the recently deceased Marjane Satrapi\, tracing themes 
 of identity\, belonging\, and displacement. Participants receive a copy of 
 Persepolis\, available for pickup at the Main Branch. We will also enjoy 
 Persian Palmers (Persian iced tea and lemonade) and cookies. \n\nPart of 
 Adult Summer Reading 2026: Unearth a Story.
