SUMMARY:Jazz Listening Session - The Music of NOW with Laurence Donahue-Greene
DESCRIPTION:Laurence Donohue-Greene is co-founder and Managing Editor of 
 The New York City Jazz Record\, easily the most important source for news\, 
 artist profiles\, record and concert reviews\, and concert listings in 
 metro NYC. As much as anyone\, Laurence has his finger on the pulse of 
 what's new and compelling in jazz and creative music. Tireless advocate\, 
 keen listener. We are fortunate to have him curate ad host this month's 
 listening session on "The Music of NOW"--the tunes that have grabbed his 
 ears\, heart and mind\, by artists whom you can catch live on a regular 
 basis. Join us to listen\, learn\, and find new artists to see in concert. 
 Going to be a great session.
LOCATION:Montclair Main - Auditorium
ORGANIZER;CN="Montclair Library":MAILTO:events@montclairlibrary.org
