SUMMARY:[MILL Senior Friday] World of Film with Mark Phelan
DESCRIPTION:Join us on Fridays for a day full of events for Seniors with 
 the MILL @ MPL! All events are free and open to the public. Registration is 
 recommended unless otherwise noted.\n\n\nPotiche (Trophy Wife) (2010) | 
 R\nIn 1977 France\, tightfisted factory owner Robert Pujol is so shocked 
 when his workers strike for higher wages that he suffers a heart attack. 
 His acquiescent wife\, Suzanne\, whose father had founded the factory\, 
 takes over management duties during Robert's convalescence. To her own 
 surprise\, Suzanne turns out to be a natural leader whose less dictatorial 
 management inspires both her workers and local liberal politician 
 Babin.\n\nABOUT THE INSTRUCTOR\nMARK PHELAN - I am a lifelong film fanatic 
 who eats\, breathes\, sleeps and drinks movies. I have studied with Donald 
 Spoto at the New School in NYC and have a BA and MA in Speech and Theatre 
 from MSU. I have also worked as an actor and have directed several plays in 
 local regional and community theaters\, including the Whole Theatre in 
 Montclair and the Paper Mill Playhouse in Millburn\, NJ. I am currently 
 working as an adjunct professor teaching\, among other courses\, 
 Introduction to Cinema.\n\nHOW TO REGISTER\nThis class is run by the MILL. 
 Please register for classes directly through their website here.\n\nFor 
 questions about MILL classes please call 973-744-3278.\n\nMILL @ MPL is 
 made possible through a partnership between the MILL\, Montclair Public 
 Library and Partners for Health.
LOCATION:Montclair Main - Auditorium
ORGANIZER;CN="Montclair Library":MAILTO:events@montclairlibrary.org
CATEGORIES:Adult Services, Books, Film & Theater
UID:LibCal-10306-16678847
URL:https://bccls.libcal.com/event/16678847
