SUMMARY:The Corner Book Club Meeting
DESCRIPTION:Join us for a lively\, librarian-led discussion of Leila 
 Mottley's critically-acclaimed debut novel\, Nightcrawling.  Kiara and her 
 brother\, Marcus\, are scraping by in an East Oakland apartment complex. 
 Both have dropped out of high school\, their family fractured by death and 
 prison…Kiara hunts for work to pay their rent—and to keep the 
 nine-year-old boy next door\, abandoned by his mother\, safe and fed. One 
 night\, what begins as a drunken misunderstanding with a stranger turns 
 into the job Kiara never imagined wanting but now desperately needs: 
 nightcrawling. \n\n
LOCATION:Montclair Bellevue Ave Branch - Classroom\, Montclair Bellevue Avenue Branch
ORGANIZER;CN="Montclair Bellevue Avenue Branch":MAILTO:branch-events@montclairlibrary.org
CATEGORIES:Book Discussion
