SUMMARY:[MILL Senior Friday] World of Film with Mark Phelan
DESCRIPTION:Join us on Fridays for a day full of events for Seniors with 
 the MILL @ MPL! All events are free and open to the public. Registration is 
 recommended unless otherwise noted.\n\n\nManhattan Murder Mystery (1993) | 
 PG\nLarry Lipton and his wife\, Carol\, are adjusting to life with their 
 son away at college when they meet their older neighbor\, Lillian House\, 
 and her husband\, Paul. Upon hearing of Lillian's sudden death\, Carol 
 grows suspicious of the circumstances surrounding her demise and comes to 
 believe Paul may have killed her. Unwilling to let her curiosity subside\, 
 she convinces Larry to join her in getting to the bottom of the 
 mystery.\n\nABOUT THE INSTRUCTOR\nMARK PHELAN - I am a lifelong film 
 fanatic who eats\, breathes\, sleeps and drinks movies. I have studied with 
 Donald Spoto at the New School in NYC and have a BA and MA in Speech and 
 Theatre from MSU. I have also worked as an actor and have directed several 
 plays in local regional and community theaters\, including the Whole 
 Theatre in Montclair and the Paper Mill Playhouse in Millburn\, NJ. I am 
 currently working as an adjunct professor teaching\, among other courses\, 
 Introduction to Cinema.\n\nHOW TO REGISTER\nThis class is run by the MILL. 
 Please register for classes directly through their website here.\n\nFor 
 questions about MILL classes please call 973-744-3278.\n\nMILL @ MPL is 
 made possible through a partnership between the MILL\, Montclair Public 
 Library and Partners for Health.
LOCATION:Montclair Main - Auditorium
ORGANIZER;CN="Montclair Library":MAILTO:events@montclairlibrary.org
CATEGORIES:Adult Services, Books, Film & Theater
