SUMMARY:[MILL Senior Friday] World of Film with Mark Phelan
DESCRIPTION:Join us on Fridays for a day full of events for Seniors with 
 the MILL @ MPL! All events are free and open to the public. Registration is 
 recommended unless otherwise noted.\n\n\nLove With the Proper Stranger 
 (1963) | NR\nAngie Rossini\, an innocent New York City sales clerk from a 
 repressive Italian-American family\, engages in a short-lived affair with a 
 handsome jazz musician named Rocky Papasano. When Angie becomes pregnant\, 
 she tracks down Rocky hoping he'll pay for her abortion. Rocky agrees to 
 help\, but after seeing the unsanitary abortion facility\, he refuses to 
 let Angie go through with the procedure and attempts to make her an honest 
 woman.\n\nABOUT THE INSTRUCTOR\nMARK PHELAN - I am a lifelong film fanatic 
 who eats\, breathes\, sleeps and drinks movies. I have studied with Donald 
 Spoto at the New School in NYC and have a BA and MA in Speech and Theatre 
 from MSU. I have also worked as an actor and have directed several plays in 
 local regional and community theaters\, including the Whole Theatre in 
 Montclair and the Paper Mill Playhouse in Millburn\, NJ. I am currently 
 working as an adjunct professor teaching\, among other courses\, 
 Introduction to Cinema.\n\nHOW TO REGISTER\nThis class is run by the MILL. 
 Please register for classes directly through their website here. This class 
 is offered both in-person and hybrid on Zoom.\n\nFor questions about MILL 
 classes please call 973-744-3278.\n\nMILL @ MPL is made possible through a 
 partnership between the MILL\, Montclair Public Library and Partners for 
 Health.
LOCATION:Montclair Main - Auditorium
ORGANIZER;CN="Montclair Library":MAILTO:events@montclairlibrary.org
CATEGORIES:Adult Services, Books, Film & Theater
UID:LibCal-10306-16678851
URL:https://bccls.libcal.com/event/16678851
END:VEVENT
